*&---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*& Report ZABAPPDF_STANDALONE
*&---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*& abapPDF: PDF form designer and native ABAP PDF renderer in one report.
*& All logic is in local classes; no other repository objects are needed.
*&
*& Installation: create program ZABAPPDF_STANDALONE in SE38, paste this
*& source and activate.
*&
*& Form storage
*& Forms are stored in table ZPDF_FORMDB when it exists (transportable, one
*& row per form version), otherwise in client-dependent INDX(ZP), ZPDF_FORMS.
*& Create ZPDF_FORMDB once in SE11 to move forms between systems:
*&   Transparent table, delivery class C, client-dependent, fields:
*&     MANDT      MANDT     key
*&     FORM_ID    CHAR 30   key
*&     VERSION    NUMC 4    key
*&     IS_ACTIVE  CHAR 1
*&     CHANGED_BY SYUNAME
*&     CHANGED_AT TIMESTAMP
*&     CONTENT    RAWSTRING (the form, compressed)
*&   Technical settings: data class APPL2, size category 0.
*& On first start the INDX forms are copied into the table (INDX is kept).
*& "Transport" in the designer adds R3TR TABU ZPDF_FORMDB with the form key
*& to a customizing request. Clients with automatic recording (SCC4) ask
*& for a request on every save; clients without changes allowed are read-only.
*& Changes are staged in memory and written under a lock when they are saved.
*& Demo: the first start on a client without forms installs form
*& ZPDF_FLIGHT_MANIFEST (printed by report ZABAPPDF_DEMO_FLIGHTS). The setup
*& runs once per client (marker INDX(ZP) ZPDF_SETUP), so deleted forms stay deleted.
*&
*& Authorization: S_PROGRAM groups ZPDFVIEW / ZPDFEDIT / ZPDFADMN.
*&
*& Template fields
*& {{FIELD}} is HTML-escaped. {{{FIELD}}} keeps only an allow-list of
*& formatting tags and attributes: scripts, frames, forms, SVG, event
*& handlers, unsafe CSS and javascript:/vbscript:/data: links are removed,
*& and images must be embedded as data:image (no external URLs).
*&
*& Engines
*& Native (default): the PDF is written in ABAP. Latin text uses the
*& standard PDF fonts; Arabic text is shaped (joined letter forms,
*& lam-alef), ordered right to left and printed with an embedded subset of
*& Noto Sans Arabic (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
*& Gotenberg (optional): a Gotenberg server converts the HTML. It is reached
*& only through the SM59 destination in gc_gotenberg_dest (no URL override).
*& Run it with --chromium-disable-javascript=true and a --chromium-deny-list
*& for internal hosts, because templates can still reference external URLs.
*& The timeout comes from the selection screen.
*&
*& API mode (for other reports)
*& EXPORT form_id json html css header footer page_size orientation
*& (strings) margin_top margin_right margin_bottom margin_left (type i)
*& TO MEMORY ID 'ZABAPPDF_API_IN', then
*& SUBMIT zabappdf_standalone WITH p_api = 'X' AND RETURN and
*& IMPORT pdf (xstring) message (string) FROM MEMORY ID 'ZABAPPDF_API_OUT'.
*&
*& Structure: local interface lif_pdf_render, then the local classes
*& (definitions first, implementations second). The user interface is an
*& HTML viewer, not dynpro modules.
*&---------------------------------------------------------------------*
REPORT zabappdf_standalone.

"Approved Gotenberg SM59 destination.
"Configure both constants together if the approved SM59 destination is renamed.
CONSTANTS gc_gotenberg_dest TYPE c LENGTH 32 VALUE 'ZPDF_GOTENBERG'.
CONSTANTS gc_gotenberg_url TYPE c LENGTH 200 VALUE 'dest://ZPDF_GOTENBERG'.

TYPE-POOLS cnht.

